{"story": {"id": "mojana", "kind": "change", "lens": "agua", "title": {"es": "Las ciénagas respiran", "en": "The wetlands breathe"}, "place": {"es": "La Mojana", "en": "La Mojana"}, "country": {"es": "Colombia", "en": "Colombia"}, "tempo": {"es": "de junio a octubre de 2026", "en": "June to October 2026"}, "center": [-74.85, 8.8], "aoi": [-75.35, 8.15, -74.25, 9.45], "stack": "011_D_084", "before": "2026-06-26", "after": "2026-10-24", "summary": {"es": "Donde el Cauca y el San Jorge se encuentran con el Magdalena, las ciénagas se llenan y se vacían con las lluvias. El radar de NISAR las sigue aunque el cielo esté cubierto.", "en": "Where the Cauca and San Jorge rivers meet the Magdalena, the wetlands fill and drain with the rains. NISAR's radar follows them even under full cloud cover."}, "steps": [{"layer": "after", "title": {"es": "Un territorio hecho de agua", "en": "A land made of water"}, "text": {"es": "En estas ciénagas, las zonas oscuras pueden corresponder a agua quieta, que refleja la señal lejos del satélite. También hay otras causas de poco retorno, como superficies lisas o sombra del radar. El brillo orienta la interpretación; no identifica por sí solo el terreno.", "en": "In these wetlands, dark areas may be still water reflecting the signal away from the satellite. Other causes of low return include smooth surfaces or radar shadow. Brightness guides interpretation; it does not identify the terrain on its own."}}, {"layer": "swipe", "title": {"es": "Dos pasadas, cuatro meses", "en": "Two passes, four months apart"}, "text": {"es": "A la izquierda, el 26 de junio; a la derecha, el 24 de octubre, en plena segunda temporada de lluvias. Mueve la cortina y fíjate en los bordes de las ciénagas.", "en": "On the left, June 26; on the right, October 24, deep into the second rainy season. Drag the curtain and watch the edges of the wetlands."}}, {"layer": "change_hh", "title": {"es": "Lo que cambió", "en": "What changed"}, "text": {"es": "En azul, donde el radar recibe menos señal que antes; en naranja, donde recibe más. El azul bordea las ciénagas: es compatible con agua que avanzó sobre sus orillas. No es una medición de inundación: es una pista para mirar más de cerca.", "en": "Blue marks where the radar now receives less signal than before; orange, where it receives more. Blue hugs the wetland edges, consistent with water spreading over their shores. This is not a flood measurement: it is a lead worth a closer look."}}, {"layer": "dance", "title": {"es": "La danza completa", "en": "The whole dance"}, "text": {"es": "NISAR volvió diez veces entre junio y octubre. Reproduce la secuencia y mira cómo late el paisaje, un compás cada doce días.", "en": "NISAR came back ten times between June and October. Play the sequence and watch the landscape pulse, one beat every twelve days."}}, {"layer": "zoom", "title": {"es": "La lupa calibrada", "en": "The calibrated lens"}, "text": {"es": "Hasta aquí usamos vistas previas, con píxeles de unos 170 metros y suavizado adicional. La lupa lee el producto científico en una ventana de 15 km: retorno calibrado y celdas de 30 metros en este caso. Se aprecian con más detalle caños, parcelas y bordes de ciénagas. Verifica las zonas señaladas con observaciones locales fechadas; el tamaño de celda no garantiza un contorno exacto.", "en": "So far we used previews with pixels about 170 metres wide and additional smoothing. The lens reads the science product over a 15 km window: calibrated return and 30-metre cells in this case. Channels, fields and wetland edges become more detailed. Check highlighted areas against dated local observations; cell size does not guarantee an exact boundary."}}], "sources": [{"label": {"es": "Misión NISAR (NASA)", "en": "NISAR mission (NASA)"}, "url": "https://science.nasa.gov/mission/nisar/"}, {"label": {"es": "Productos GCOV en ASF", "en": "GCOV products at ASF"}, "url": "https://nisar-docs.asf.alaska.edu/gcov/"}], "lupa": {"lon": -74.85, "lat": 8.72, "size_km": 15}}, "stack": {"id": "011_D_084", "track": 11, "frame": 84, "direction": "DESCENDING", "polarizations": ["HH", "HV"], "footprint": {"type": "Polygon", "coordinates": [[[-76.10737, 10.22198], [-76.59117, 8.13493], [-74.32955, 7.61094], [-73.83957, 9.6908], [-76.10737, 10.22198]]]}, "first": "2025-10-29", "last": "2026-10-24", "analyzable_count": 10, "scenes": [{"id": "G4058281995-ASF", "granule": "NISAR_L2_PR_GCOV_004_011_D_084_4005_DHDH_A_20251029T232805_20251029T232839_X05009_N_F_J_001", "date": "2025-10-29", "datetime": "2025-10-29T23:28:05Z", "cycle": 4, "mode": "4005_DHDH", "collection": "NISAR_L2_GCOV_BETA_V1", "quality": "beta", "analyzable": false, "thumbnail": null}, {"id": "G4058418120-ASF", "granule": "NISAR_L2_PR_GCOV_006_011_D_084_4005_DHDH_A_20251122T232805_20251122T232840_X05009_N_F_J_001", "date": "2025-11-22", "datetime": "2025-11-22T23:28:05Z", "cycle": 6, "mode": "4005_DHDH", "collection": "NISAR_L2_GCOV_BETA_V1", "quality": "beta", "analyzable": false, "thumbnail": null}, {"id": "G4058494021-ASF", "granule": "NISAR_L2_PR_GCOV_007_011_D_084_4005_DHDH_A_20251204T232806_20251204T232840_X05009_N_F_J_001", "date": "2025-12-04", "datetime": "2025-12-04T23:28:06Z", "cycle": 7, "mode": "4005_DHDH", "collection": "NISAR_L2_GCOV_BETA_V1", "quality": "beta", "analyzable": false, "thumbnail": null}, {"id": "G4058628726-ASF", "granule": "NISAR_L2_PR_GCOV_008_011_D_084_4005_DHDH_A_20251216T232807_20251216T232841_X05009_N_F_J_001", "date": "2025-12-16", "datetime": "2025-12-16T23:28:07Z", "cycle": 8, "mode": "4005_DHDH", "collection": "NISAR_L2_GCOV_BETA_V1", "quality": "beta", "analyzable": false, "thumbnail": null}, {"id": "G4058739108-ASF", "granule": "NISAR_L2_PR_GCOV_009_011_D_084_4005_DHDH_A_20251228T232807_20251228T232841_X05009_N_F_J_001", "date": "2025-12-28", "datetime": "2025-12-28T23:28:07Z", "cycle": 9, "mode": "4005_DHDH", "collection": "NISAR_L2_GCOV_BETA_V1", "quality": "beta", "analyzable": false, "thumbnail": null}, {"id": "G4059060403-ASF", "gr